scene('capability-contract','One action has a promise and an engine','The contract [capability.ts] says what the action accepts and returns. The binding [implementation.ts] supplies target metadata and executable code.','TypeScript target describes dispatch. Its handler can still call a model.',contract_drawing(ACTIONS['find_times']),contract_steps(ACTIONS['find_times']),'PK02 PK03 PK04 PK08 PK13 PK38 PK42 FINDC FINDI BOOKC STAFF SALESSOURCE','ClinicOS uses defineCapability for typed contract data and bindCapability for contract + target + run. Its local helper narrows target to TypeScript, while Core also accepts agent, team, work and reserved Core handlers. Sales agent:sales targets a runtime whose mounted capability channel dispatches ordinary run code; this does not itself require a conversational LLM turn. A TypeScript handler can call Core’s authorized model broker. Contract identity, implementation target and actual internal reasoning are separate facts.',variants(contract_drawing,contract_steps))

