scene('capability-lifecycle','Installed here, governed here','The generated action must be published, installed and enabled here. Finding it still does not authorize execution.','Published, found, ready, allowed and completed are independent states.',lifecycle_drawing(ACTIONS['find_times']),lifecycle_steps(ACTIONS['find_times']),'PK01 PK18 PK19 PK20 PK21 PK22 PK23 PK24 PK25 PK26 PK27 PK28 PK29 PK30 PK32 PK34 PK39 PK50','Core exact ID is pack slug + slash + contract key. Publishing persists immutable contract snapshots and computed closure. Closure unions declared action, implementing agent/team and declared tools requirements; it is metadata, not static analysis of helper calls. TypeScript contributes its own listed requirements. Active install creates bindings; widening approved access can hold consent, while existing choices survive resync. Search can find unready or approval-required candidates. Invocation rechecks, mints narrowed runtime authority, validates output and prevents a late response from replacing reclaimed uncertainty. No live install/deployed version was checked.',lifevars)

