scene('capability-examples','Find a time, then book that time','Two actions inside ClinicOS compose through exact slot fields. Finding a time does not secretly call booking.','The operator composes actions; each keeps its own contract, policy and outcome.',example_svg,example_steps,'FINDC FINDI FINDMED BOOKC BOOKREQ STAFF BOOK PK38 PK49','Find open times [clinic.find_times] requires procedure and returns times plus optional service/range/context fields. Exact times carry starts_at, ends_at, practitioner_ref, when, minutes, with; service/mode accompany the response. It uses Medplum/Brain/settings/work_items, approval allow, timeout 30s. It does not change appointments but can raise setup work; it is not in the hardcoded read-only deadline allowlist. Book [clinic.book] adds person identity, requires exact fields, has approval_required, preview and a 60s budget. Preview uses no-write authority; execution checks fresh conditions then shared bookTime verifies provider truth. Output includes appointment_ref, starts_at, when, already_booked, look_alike and confirmation. Timeout constants are not latency measurements. Patient tools and booking page use shared helpers under separate authority; they are not universally routed through staff clinic.book.',examplevars)

